<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2014/Dandelion.jpg" alt="A portrait painting of a rabbit done on toned canvas. The background has been left unpainted." width="450" height="325" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Dandelion. 9x12, oil on linen panel. 2014</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">To be honest, it is difficult to keep finding a name for rabbit paintings so I've decided that I will just have to rely on my imagination a little more.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">I found this rabbit by going for a 2.5 mile walk down some of the unpaved country roads round our neck of the woods armed with my camera and a long lens.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">I did the painting in a fairly straightforward way, sketching in the form gesturally with raw umber and separating out the light and dark areas before applying the final layers directly over the top.</p>